Vendored from alphaXiv/OpenResearch v0.1.120, the CLAUDE_SKILL constant in
src/local/harness/mod.rs, unmodified.

This is the same shim `orx install-skills` would write to
~/.claude/skills/orx/SKILL.md. That command is not run here: ~/.claude is
generated by homes/programs/claude-code.nix, so an imperative write there is
either clobbered on the next rebuild or fails against the read-only store. The
file is carried in-tree instead and installed through `skills` in
homes/programs/ai-skills.nix.

Only the shim is vendored, not the eleven modules under the upstream
`agent-skills/` directory (`orx install-skills --full`). The shim's whole job is
to tell the agent to run `orx skill`, which prints the current manual straight
out of the installed binary - so the guidance tracks the CLI version
automatically and this file does not go stale between releases. Upstream makes
the same call: --full is "intended for dedicated/orx-only environments. In a
general-purpose setup the always-on skills add noise, so the default is the
shim alone."

